  "route": "cardiff",
  "title": "Cardiff City Network: busy weekday",
  "description": "A busier weekday on the Cardiff Valley Lines and through Cardiff Central: peak-level frequencies all day, more main-line trains and freight (tsw-schedule). Times are approximate.",
  "notes": "Based on the typical weekday, with extra trains in the gaps of the standard hour: Valleys to Cardiff Central every 15 minutes; an extra Rhymney line train each way through to Barry; a second London - Swansea each way; Ebbw Vale trains hourly; steel trains hourly each way. The Cardiff Bay shuttle stays every 12 minutes (one unit on the single-track branch). Every portal has at least 3 minutes between entries.",
